### RUN .setup for group B (oper-2026-10-22T1122): AWPTCM-T33401 Syslog Facility Override,
### AWPTCM-T33402 Syslog stored in NVS, AWPTCM-T33403 Scripting.
### Declares ONLY swi_d (u2, the DUT), per STANDING-ORDERS §6.
###
### This session's dispatch gives `consoles: u2 ONLY`. swi_b (u3) and swi_a (u5) are NOT
### opened: CK_PASSWORD_U3 / CK_PASSWORD_U5 are absent from this session's environment, and a
### console driver that falls back to default passwords is a lockout generator (AW+ locks at
### five failures and every further failure re-arms the five-minute timer -- that is what
### locked swi_b on 2026-10-21). The Test Engineer's answer was "DUT only -- don't open u3/u5".
### Both units are therefore absent from this file entirely -- no [switch], no [baudrates],
### no [power], no [powerlink], no [boot_from_flash] and no [portlink] touching them. With no
### entry at all, the framework's post-failure power cycle can never reach either unit.
###
### All three partner roles these cases need are played by the TESTBOX ITSELF:
###   T33401 -- the syslog collector is a bounded `tcpdump ... udp port 514` capture on the
###             box's eth3 leg (10.38.22.33), cabled to swi_d port1.0.10 (vlan10). No UDP :514
###             listener exists on tb277 and none is needed: the verdict rests on the received
###             PRI byte decoded from the capture, not on any daemon's stored file.
###   T33402 -- entirely on the DUT (write + reload + read back).
###   T33403 -- the .scp is staged in the box's /tftproot (mode 1777, tftpd-hpa active) and
###             pulled by the DUT with `copy tftp://10.38.22.33/<f>.scp flash:/<f>.scp`.
### Not a partner switch anywhere.
### The box has NO deployed /home/st-art/configs/tb277.setup; never bind one.

[power]
pwr_d = (pdu, 10.36.230.212, 1)

[switch]
swi_d = /dev/u2

[baudrates]
swi_d = 115200

[stack]

[configured_stackport]

[powerlink]
swi_d = pwr_d

[boot_from_flash]
swi_d = True

[portlink]
tb-swi_d = eth3-port1.0.10, eth4-port1.0.48
